The block below is an unverified guess: no repository files were included, so I wrote the SEARCH text from my memory of the GitHub CLI source in `api/client.go`. I have not run it or checked it against the file.

The assumed cause is that `RESTWithNext`, the paginated path, returns the go-gh library's HTTP error as-is. That is a different type from the CLI's own `HTTPError`, so type checks on the paginated path fail. Passing the error through `handleResponse` should give the CLI's `HTTPError` type, with the same status code and scope guidance as `REST`. That in turn should let the status command tolerate a 404 and the attestation commands retry on a 500.

If `RESTWithNext` or `handleResponse` looks different in your tree, the SEARCH text will not match and the block will need adjusting.

